00:09:00.964 --> 00:09:06.164
Take the supply rail down near the point where a transistor only just turns on, and a small

00:09:06.164 --> 00:09:10.284
sag stretches delay far more than the same sag would on a normal voltage.

00:09:11.444 --> 00:09:16.284
Semiconductor engineering's account of edge AI chips puts that region at about 4 tenths

00:09:16.284 --> 00:09:18.924
to half a volt in advanced FinFET processes.

00:09:19.544 --> 00:09:24.504
Energy per switch falls with the rail, and because dynamic energy follows the square of voltage,

00:09:24.504 --> 00:09:30.424
the same activity costs sharply less. Delay grows fast, part-to-part variation

00:09:30.424 --> 00:09:36.644
widens, noise margin shrinks, timing paths feel small voltage moves, IR drop and

00:09:36.644 --> 00:09:41.304
local droop become first order. A guard band drawn at the nominal voltage stops

00:09:41.304 --> 00:09:46.324
telling you what the silicon will do, and a model taken there misses the part. Memory

00:09:46.324 --> 00:09:50.864
usually sets how far you can go. A single rail memory with a cyst that has been

00:09:50.864 --> 00:09:56.744
checked on silicon can hold a minimum around 600 mV, so you take the voltage-squared saving

00:09:56.744 --> 00:09:57.964
without splitting the grid.

00:09:58.504 --> 00:10:02.964
A dual-rail memory lets logic drop while the array stays high enough to hold state.

00:10:03.504 --> 00:10:07.604
The same account points to an ISSCC-2025 result.

00:10:08.144 --> 00:10:17.364
A dual-rail SRAM at 38 Mbps square mm, logic at 380 mV, the memory rail at 540 mV, in

00:10:17.364 --> 00:10:18.864
a 3 nanometer finfet.

00:10:18.864 --> 00:10:22.464
Small register files sit next to the compute for local data.

00:10:23.044 --> 00:10:26.284
Multiply accumulate tiles want small distributed SRAM.

00:10:26.804 --> 00:10:29.864
Activation units want those register files on wide paths.

00:10:30.584 --> 00:10:33.264
Shared buffers want a high band with AXI port.

00:10:33.804 --> 00:10:36.404
The cell library has to be characterized for that band.

00:10:36.944 --> 00:10:42.964
Moment-based LVF timing and noise models across a wide process, voltage and temperature range,

00:10:43.444 --> 00:10:48.844
delay and slew models that catch the nonlinear sensitivity, and extra checks for MISFF

00:10:48.844 --> 00:10:53.624
pulse width, skew, and mixed devices, because the noise margin is thin.

00:10:54.504 --> 00:10:57.744
Silicon sweeps on timing and function are what keep the models honest.

00:10:58.444 --> 00:11:00.224
The I-O can veto the whole plan.

00:11:00.784 --> 00:11:13.004
GPIO I-3C, I-2C, SWI-3S, LVDS, RGMII, clocks, SD and EMMC, test pins, and the 2.5D or 3D

00:11:13.004 --> 00:11:16.784
links for chiplets each have to behave across the supplies the core wants.

00:11:16.784 --> 00:11:21.964
If they cannot, the periphery sets the chip's minimum voltage, and the low voltage core

00:11:21.964 --> 00:11:23.344
never shows up in the product.

00:11:23.744 --> 00:11:29.304
The account says a closed loop of foundation IP, design tools and silicon feedback is

00:11:29.304 --> 00:11:34.184
what makes 4 tents to half a volt predictable, and those blocks have to be chosen early.

00:11:34.744 --> 00:11:39.264
That rail stops earning its place when the memory, or the IO, cannot follow the compute

00:11:39.264 --> 00:11:44.924
supply down, or when the extra delay and variation force guard bands that hand back the energy

00:11:44.924 --> 00:11:49.944
the lower voltage was supposed to buy. Then a split rail, or a supply held above the

00:11:49.944 --> 00:11:55.084
sharp part of the delay curve, is what keeps a real-time edge job inside its timing budget.

